namespace trion:
    use formal

    source CLOSED-CASE-COVERAGE:
        title "Coverage of values in closed attributes"
        locator "urn:trion:verification:closed-case-coverage"
        kind citation
        quote RULES """
Consider each closed attribute that appears in a condition. For each listed value, substitute that value for the tests of the attribute in every condition that mentions it. Evaluate the Boolean connectives with the other tests unknown. Report a missing case only when all those conditions are definitely false. This warning describes the coverage of the conditions.
"""

    section "What a verification answers":
        A verification means an examination of a specification by the trioc command.
        A verification result means the answer of a verification.
        The verdict of a verification result is consistent, inconsistent, or unknown.
        Each verification result names the bounds of the verification.

        [VERIFY-BOUND-NAMED]
        If a verification reaches a bound, then the trioc command shall name the bound in the verification result.

        [VERIFY-UNKNOWN]
        If a verification stops before the verdict of the verification result, then the trioc command shall report the verdict "unknown".

        [VERIFY-UNKNOWN-NO-SUCCESS]
        The trioc command shall not accept a specification whose verdict is "unknown".

    section "Consistency":
        ref [SENTENCE-INPUT-ENABLED]

        [VERIFY-CONSISTENCY]
        If a specification has a conflict, then the trioc command shall report the specification as inconsistent.

        [VERIFY-CONFLICT-NAMED]
        The trioc command shall name each statement of each conflict.

        example CONFLICT-UNDER-A-CONDITION:
            kind consistency
            input """
[D] The door is open or closed.
[A] While the door is open, the lamp shall be lit.
[B] While the door is open, the lamp shall not be lit.
"""
            expect inconsistent

        A guarantee sentence excludes no input.
        An assumption sentence excludes each input that fails the assumption sentence.

        example CONDITIONS-TOGETHER:
            kind consistency
            input """
[A] When a user sends a message, the API shall store the message.
[B] While the room is archived, the API shall not store the message.
"""
            expect inconsistent

        example CONDITIONS-EXCLUDED:
            kind consistency
            input """
[A] While the door is open, the fan shall run.
[B] While the alarm is active, the fan shall not run.
[C] While the door is open, the alarm is never active.
"""
            expect consistent

        example EVENTS-AT-ONE-MOMENT:
            kind consistency
            input """
[A] When the door opens, the API shall stop.
[B] When the bell rings, the API shall not stop.
[C] When the bell rings, no door opens.
"""
            expect inconsistent

    section "The reactive reading of consistency":
        ref [OBLIGATION-REALIZABILITY]

        [VERIFY-REALIZABILITY]
        If a guarantee requires a response before a free occurrence, then the trion processor shall write a realizability obligation for the response.

    section "Compatibility":
        ref [OBLIGATION-COMPATIBILITY]
        [VERIFY-COMPATIBILITY]
        If a specification admits no input, then the trioc command shall report the specification as incompatible.

    section "Correctness and completeness against a reference":
        ref [OBLIGATION-CORRECTNESS]
        ref [OBLIGATION-COMPLETENESS]

        [VERIFY-CORRECTNESS]
        The trion processor shall write the proof obligation of the correctness of a specification against each reference of the specification.

        [VERIFY-COMPLETENESS]
        If a specification has a gap, then the trioc command shall report the specification as incomplete.

        [VERIFY-NO-REFERENCE]
        The trioc command shall not report the completeness of a specification that has no reference.

    section "Missing cases":
        A closed attribute means an attribute that an enumeration closes.
        An open attribute means an attribute that no enumeration closes.
        A missing case means a value of a closed attribute that the conditions of the specification exclude from their coverage.
            cite CLOSED-CASE-COVERAGE#RULES
        A missing case differs from an incomplete specification.

        [VERIFY-MISSING-CASE]
        If a specification has a missing case, then the trion processor shall report the missing case.

        [VERIFY-OPEN-DOMAIN]
        Each missing case that the trion processor reports shall be a value of a closed attribute.

    section "Expected properties":
        ref [OBLIGATION-EXPECTED-PROPERTY]
        The outcome of a check is proved, refuted, or unknown.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY]
        The trion processor shall write the proof obligation of each check of a specification.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-PROVED]
        If the outcome of a check is proved, then the trioc command shall accept the check.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-REFUTED]
        If the outcome of a check is refuted, then the trioc command shall report the check as an error.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-UNKNOWN]
        If the outcome of a check is unknown, then the trioc command shall report the check as unproved.
